window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-20bc98306a44b420"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"plugin-controls\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">插件控制</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>插件可以打包可重复使用的工作流，并可包含技能和用于连接其他工具的 MCP 服务器。在受支持的界面中，ChatGPT 和 Codex 使用同一个公开插件目录；管理员决定工作区中可使用哪些插件。了解更多关于<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>、<a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">技能</a>和<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11487775\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">已连接服务（需联网）</a>的信息。</p> <p>有关工作区控制和数据处理的指导，请参阅帮助中心中的 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件和应用的管理员控制、安全与合规（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>在本指南中，<strong>app</strong>（应用）和 <strong>MCP server</strong>（MCP 服务器）指同一种已连接集成，两者可以互换使用。正文中使用 <strong>MCP server</strong>，但界面标签（如 <strong>Workspace apps</strong> 和 <strong>App permissions</strong>）以及 CSV 列名仍保留 <strong>app</strong>。</p> <p>只有当插件和 MCP 服务器对成员的角色开放，并且已验证身份的账户可以访问相应已连接服务时，成员才能使用该服务器的能力。对于共享凭据，成员还必须有权使用该凭据；外部服务账户也可能与其个人账户不同。</p> <p>插件可在 ChatGPT 网页版、桌面版和移动版的 Chat 与 Work 中使用，也可在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 Codex 以及 Codex CLI 插件浏览器中使用。IDE 扩展不支持插件。</p> <p>要了解这些控制项如何与工作区角色和权限配合，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">角色与工作区权限</a>。</p> <p>要为受支持的工作区体验配置插件身份验证，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">工作区连接</a>。仅仅为所有人安装插件，并不会自动提供共享账户。</p> <p>Sites 中的插件让每位访客使用自己的已连接账户。每个插件都有独立的 Sites 权限，其默认值取决于工作区套餐。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df?sectionMissing=enable-plugin-use-in-sites\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">在 Sites 中启用插件（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>，了解插件默认设置、访问权限更改和租户限制排查。</p> <p><a id=\"understand-the-capability-chain\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">了解能力控制链</h2> <p>插件可能涉及以下控制层：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>层级</th> <th>决定的内容</th> <th>管理位置</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>可用性</td> <td>用户能否使用该插件包</td> <td>受支持的网页和桌面界面使用<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/settings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">工作区设置（需联网）</a>；CLI 使用插件浏览器</td> </tr> <tr> <td>内含技能</td> <td>已安装插件提供哪些可重复使用的指令</td> <td>插件包和<a href=\"#/article/a-160e62101398766a\">技能控制</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>MCP 服务器访问权</td> <td>用户能否使用 MCP 服务器的能力</td> <td><a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Workspace apps（需联网）</a> 和 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/settings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Permissions &amp; roles（需联网）</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>操作与权限</td> <td>用户可以执行哪些操作，以及 ChatGPT 何时会在使用工具前询问</td> <td>连接的 <strong>Action control</strong> 和 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Workspace apps（需联网）</a> 中的 <strong>App permissions</strong></td> </tr> <tr> <td>服务授权</td> <td>已验证身份可以访问哪些外部数据和操作</td> <td>已连接服务及其身份提供方</td> </tr> <tr> <td>运行时权限</td> <td>智能体收到数据或工具后可以执行什么操作</td> <td>当前界面的运行时、沙盒和审批控制项</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>可将这些层级用于两步式上线：先开放合适的插件，再配置每个工作流所需的能力与权限。</p> <p><a id=\"step-1-enable-plugin-availability\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"1\">第 1 步：启用插件可用性</h2> <p>对于受支持的网页和桌面界面，工作区插件控制项决定哪些角色可以使用或安装插件。Codex CLI 使用自己的插件浏览器进行安装。有关打包和分发的信息，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建插件</a>。</p> <p>要从 GitHub 导入工作区插件并保持更新，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-ab115ea47731f92a\">插件管理</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"export-the-public-catalog-for-review\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">导出公开目录以供审查</h3> <p>符合条件的 ChatGPT Enterprise 工作区所有者和管理员可以下载一份 CSV，查看其工作区可用的公开插件。在更改插件可用性之前，可用这份导出文件检查插件、MCP 服务器和技能元数据。</p> <ol> <li>打开 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin &gt; Plugins（需联网）</a>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Public</strong>。</li> <li>在页面标题栏选择下载图标（<strong>Export CSV</strong>）。</li> </ol> <p>下载文件名为 <code>public-plugins-security-review.csv</code>，包含：</p> <ul> <li>插件元数据：<code>Plugin Name</code>、<code>Plugin Description</code>、<code>Date Added (UTC)</code>、<code>OpenAI Verified</code>、<code>Developer Name</code> 和 <code>Version</code>。</li> <li>MCP 服务器元数据：<code>App Name(s)</code> 和 <code>App Description(s)</code>。</li> <li>Chat 技能元数据：<code>Skill Name(s)</code> 和 <code>Skill Description(s)</code>。</li> </ul> <p>如果一个插件包含多个 MCP 服务器或技能，相应值之间以分号分隔。导出内容使用的公开目录快照最多可能滞后 48 小时，只包含当前工作区可见的公开插件，不包含为该工作区创建的插件。FedRAMP 工作区无法使用此功能。</p> <p><a id=\"step-2-manage-capabilities\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"2\">第 2 步：管理能力</h2> <p>对话同步不会授予额外的插件、MCP 服务器或已连接服务访问权限。对于 Work Cloud 本地计算机访问，Agent Security 的企业级 <code>apps</code> 和 <code>plugins</code> 要求适用于本地执行器。Work 云容器继续遵循现有 Work Cloud 策略。请通过 TOML 配置这些要求，并结合工作区权限和已连接账户的权限一并审查。</p> <p>请将钩子支持情况与插件可用性分开检查：</p> <ul> <li><strong>企业钩子。</strong> 如果工作区已启用，Work Cloud 本地计算机访问支持由管理员定义、在云端协调器（orchestrator）上运行的 MCP hooks，用于受支持的生命周期和工具事件。即使工具在本地执行，云端编排也不支持命令钩子、来自本地配置的钩子或插件钩子。</li> <li><strong>云端编排：</strong> 即使工具在本地执行且插件已获准，命令钩子、来自本地配置的钩子或插件钩子都不会运行。此功能不支持消费者用户使用钩子。如果编排和执行都在本地，现有受支持的钩子仍可用于仅本地运行的 Work 和 Codex 对话。管理员仍可在 Agent Security 中为这些工作流配置受支持的托管钩子。</li> <li><strong>审计。</strong> 依赖这些钩子前，请测试回调连接、确认它能接收哪些事件，并检查失败会如何影响任务。MCP hooks 不能提供完整的 Compliance API 审计记录。</li> </ul> <p>有关受支持的要求，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4\">Hooks</a> 和<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p> <p>在 ChatGPT 中开放 MCP 服务器或插件，并不会授予其访问已连接服务中文件、记录或操作的权限。排查访问问题时，请检查成员的工作区角色和已批准的操作设置，再确认已验证账户或共享连接在已连接服务中具有预期权限。</p> <p>ChatGPT 和 Codex 中的插件可以包含 MCP 服务器连接，用于搜索、检索、同步或操作外部系统。插件是否可用，以及各连接获准的访问范围和操作权限，是彼此独立的控制项。</p> <p>通过 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Workspace apps（需联网）</a> 和 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/settings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Permissions &amp; roles（需联网）</a> 管理 MCP 服务器能力。管理员可以：</p> <ul> <li>启用 MCP 服务器连接，并按工作区角色分配访问权。</li> <li>对支持 <strong>Action control</strong> 的连接，只允许只读操作或一组获准操作，并指定如何处理后来新增的操作。</li> <li>设置 <strong>App permissions</strong>，决定 ChatGPT 在使用连接前何时需要询问。</li> <li>将访问范围限制在已连接服务和已验证账户授予的范围与权限内。</li> </ul> <p>当前可用性和操作步骤请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">应用中的管理员控制、安全与合规（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"restrict-company-app-accounts-to-authorized-workspaces\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">将公司应用账户限制在获准的工作区中</h2> <p>启用经过验证的域名限制后，用户将无法在个人 ChatGPT 工作区或其他未授权工作区中，使用公司域名账户新建对受支持应用的连接。员工必须在获准的工作区中连接这些公司账户。</p> <p>验证域名本身不会启用此限制。现有应用连接也不会因此自动断开。</p> <p>有关受支持应用、可用性和设置说明，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件和应用的管理员控制、安全与合规（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-starting-set-of-apps\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-focused-initial-set\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">选择精简的初始应用集合</h2> <p>启用能够支持已批准业务需求的插件。将每个插件的使用对象设为确实需要它的用户或角色，并在启用前完成所需审查。</p> <p>对于每项已连接服务，请记录业务负责人、允许访问的数据、已批准的读取或写入操作、身份验证方式，以及支持或移除联系人的信息。</p> <p>启用写入操作或发布新的连接能力前，请核实其角色范围，并使用仅具备预期服务权限的账户进行测试。</p> <p>大范围推广时，可先从团队每天都会用到的类别开始，例如电子邮件、日历、文件或文档系统。通过 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Plugins Directory（需联网）</a> 查看 ChatGPT 和 Codex 受支持界面当前提供的插件及能力。</p> <p>无论初始选择是什么，都应先从读取操作开始。启用写入操作前，请确认插件负责人、审查 MCP 服务器范围和服务权限、核实数据访问范围，并记录外部影响及恢复方案。</p> <p><a id=\"understand-data-flow-and-security\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">了解数据流与安全性</h2> <p>ChatGPT 使用插件中的 MCP 服务器时，会向已连接服务发送请求，并返回该服务中已验证账户权限所允许的数据或操作结果。</p> <p>ChatGPT 以两种方式处理已连接服务的数据：</p> <ul> <li><strong>不同步：</strong> ChatGPT 会临时处理 Chat 和深度研究中的数据，但不会为其建立索引。</li> <li><strong>同步：</strong> ChatGPT 会提前为选定的已连接内容建立索引。你可以在插件页面查看某个连接是否支持同步。</li> </ul> <p>两种模式的区别在于 ChatGPT 如何为已连接内容建立索引，不会取代常规聊天保留控制。使用这些连接的 ChatGPT 对话仍可通过 Compliance API 访问。</p> <p>OpenAI 关于已连接服务的指导说明：Business、Enterprise 和 Edu 客户的数据在传输和静态存储时会加密，按用户授权，并提供角色和操作控制；使用这些连接的对话受到网络访问限制，且不会使用通过这些连接访问的信息训练模型。当请求到达已连接服务时，该服务自身的范围、保留、数据驻留及其他政策也适用。</p> <p>另请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">已连接服务的安全与合规（需联网）</a>和<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10847137\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">支持同步的连接（需联网）</a>，了解当前数据处理详情。若要在 ChatGPT 桌面应用、Codex CLI 或 IDE 扩展中配置本地 MCP 服务器，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Codex MCP 配置</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"use-current-procedures-and-references\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">使用最新操作指南与参考资料</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">应用中的管理员控制、安全与合规（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11487775\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 中的应用（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10847137\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">支持同步的应用（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">管理工作区设置（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">技能与插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">管理员推广指南</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"plugin-controls\">Plugin controls</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Plugins package reusable workflows and can include skills and MCP servers that connect to other tools. ChatGPT and Codex use the same public plugin directory on supported surfaces, while admins decide which plugins are available in their workspace. Learn more about <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">plugins</a>, <a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">skills</a>, and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11487775\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">connected services (online)</a>.</p> <p>For workspace controls and data-handling guidance, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin controls, security, and compliance for plugins and apps (online)</a> in the Help Center.</p> <p>In this guide, <strong>app</strong> and <strong>MCP server</strong> refer to the same connected integration and are interchangeable terms. We use <strong>MCP server</strong> in the prose, but preserve <strong>app</strong> in UI labels such as <strong>Workspace apps</strong> and <strong>App permissions</strong>, and in CSV column names.</p> <p>A member can use an MCP server's capabilities only when the plugin and MCP server are available to their role and the authenticated account has access to the connected service. For a shared credential, the member also needs permission to use that credential; the external account can differ from their personal account.</p> <p>Plugins work in Chat and Work across ChatGPT on the web, desktop, and mobile, in Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app, and through the Codex CLI plugin browser. They aren't available in the IDE extension.</p> <p>To see how these controls fit with workspace roles and permissions, see <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">Roles and workspace permissions</a>.</p> <p>To configure plugin authentication for supported workspace experiences, see <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1\">Workspace connections</a>. Installing a plugin for everyone doesn't, by itself, provide a shared account.</p> <p>Plugins in Sites let each visitor use their own connected accounts. Each plugin has a separate Sites permission, with defaults that depend on the workspace plan. See <a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df?sectionMissing=enable-plugin-use-in-sites\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">Enable plugin use in Sites (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> to review plugin defaults, change access, and troubleshoot tenant restrictions.</p> <h2 id=\"understand-the-capability-chain\">Understand the capability chain</h2> <p>A plugin can span these control layers:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Layer</th> <th>What it determines</th> <th>Where to manage it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Availability</td> <td>Whether the plugin bundle is available to the user</td> <td><a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/settings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Workspace settings (online)</a> for supported web and desktop surfaces; the CLI plugin browser for CLI</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Included skills</td> <td>Which reusable instructions the installed plugin contributes</td> <td>The plugin package and <a href=\"#/article/a-160e62101398766a\">Skill controls</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>MCP server access</td> <td>Whether users can use an MCP server's capabilities</td> <td><a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Workspace apps (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/settings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Permissions &amp; roles (online)</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Actions and permissions</td> <td>Which actions users can run and when ChatGPT asks before using its tools</td> <td>The connection's <strong>Action control</strong> and <strong>App permissions</strong> in <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Workspace apps (online)</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Service authorization</td> <td>Which external data and actions the authenticated identity can access</td> <td>The connected service and its identity provider</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Runtime permissions</td> <td>What an agent can do after it receives data or a tool</td> <td>The runtime, sandbox, and approval controls for the active surface</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Use these layers as a two-step rollout: first make the right plugins available, then configure the capabilities and permissions each workflow needs.</p> <h2 id=\"step-1-enable-plugin-availability\">Step 1: Enable plugin availability</h2> <p>For supported web and desktop surfaces, workspace plugin controls determine which roles can use or install a plugin. The Codex CLI uses its own plugin browser for installation. See <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build plugins</a> for packaging and distribution.</p> <p>To import workspace plugins from GitHub and keep them up to date, see <a href=\"#/article/a-ab115ea47731f92a\">Plugin management</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"export-the-public-catalog-for-review\">Export the public catalog for review</h3> <p>Eligible ChatGPT Enterprise workspace owners and admins can download a CSV of the public plugins available to their workspace. Use the export to review plugin, MCP server, and skill metadata before changing plugin availability.</p> <ol> <li>Open <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin &gt; Plugins (online)</a>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Public</strong>.</li> <li>Select the download icon (<strong>Export CSV</strong>) in the page header.</li> </ol> <p>The download uses the filename <code>public-plugins-security-review.csv</code> and includes:</p> <ul> <li>Plugin metadata: <code>Plugin Name</code>, <code>Plugin Description</code>, <code>Date Added (UTC)</code>, <code>OpenAI Verified</code>, <code>Developer Name</code>, and <code>Version</code>.</li> <li>MCP server metadata: <code>App Name(s)</code> and <code>App Description(s)</code>.</li> <li>Chat skill metadata: <code>Skill Name(s)</code> and <code>Skill Description(s)</code>.</li> </ul> <p>When a plugin includes more than one MCP server or skill, semicolons separate the corresponding values. The export uses a public-catalog snapshot that can be up to 48 hours old, includes only public plugins visible to the current workspace, and does not include plugins created for that workspace. It isn't available in FedRAMP workspaces.</p> <h2 id=\"step-2-manage-capabilities\">Step 2: Manage capabilities</h2> <p>Conversation sync does not grant additional plugin, MCP server, or connected-service access. For Local computer access with Work Cloud, Agent Security's enterprise <code>apps</code> and <code>plugins</code> requirements apply to local executors. Work cloud containers retain existing Work Cloud policies. Configure these requirements through TOML and review them alongside workspace permissions and the connected account's permissions.</p> <p>Review hook support separately from plugin availability:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Enterprise hooks.</strong> Where enabled for your workspace, Local computer access with Work Cloud supports admin-defined MCP hooks that run on the cloud coordinator (orchestrator) for supported lifecycle and tool events. Command hooks and hooks from local configuration or plugins are not supported with cloud orchestration, even when tools execute locally.</li> <li><strong>Cloud orchestration:</strong> Command hooks and hooks from local configuration or plugins do not run, even when tools execute locally and the plugin itself is allowed. Consumers do not have hooks support in this feature. When both orchestration and execution are local, existing supported hooks continue to work in local-only Work and Codex threads. Admins can still configure supported managed hooks in Agent Security for those workflows.</li> <li><strong>Auditing.</strong> Before relying on these hooks, test the callback connection, confirm the events it receives, and check how failures affect the task. MCP hooks do not provide a complete Compliance API audit trail.</li> </ul> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4\">Hooks</a> and the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Configuration Reference</a> for supported requirements.</p> <p>Making an MCP server or plugin available in ChatGPT doesn't grant access to files, records, or actions in the connected service. When troubleshooting access, check the member's workspace role and approved action settings. Then confirm the authenticated account or shared connection has the expected permissions in the connected service.</p> <p>Plugins in ChatGPT and Codex can include MCP server connections that search, retrieve, sync, or act on external systems. Plugin availability and the access and actions granted to each connection are separate controls.</p> <p>Manage MCP server capabilities from <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Workspace apps (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/settings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Permissions &amp; roles (online)</a>. Available controls let admins:</p> <ul> <li>Enable MCP server connections and assign access by workspace role.</li> <li>For connections that support <strong>Action control</strong>, allow read-only actions or an approved custom set, including how the workspace handles newly added actions.</li> <li>Set <strong>App permissions</strong> that determine when ChatGPT asks before using a connection.</li> <li>Keep access within the scopes and permissions granted by each connected service and authenticated account.</li> </ul> <p>For current availability and procedures, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin controls, security, and compliance in apps (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"restrict-company-app-accounts-to-authorized-workspaces\">Restrict company app accounts to authorized workspaces</h2> <p>When activated, verified-domain restrictions prevent users from creating new connections to supported apps with company-domain accounts in personal ChatGPT workspaces or other unauthorized workspaces. Employees must use an authorized workspace to connect those company accounts.</p> <p>Verifying a domain does not activate this restriction. Existing app connections are not automatically disconnected.</p> <p>For supported apps, availability, and setup guidance, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin controls, security, and compliance for plugins and apps (online)</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-starting-set-of-apps\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"choose-a-focused-initial-set\">Choose a focused initial set</h2> <p>Enable plugins that support an approved business need. Set each plugin’s audience to the users or roles that need it, and complete any required review before enabling it.</p> <p>For each connected service, record the business owner, permitted data, approved read or write actions, authentication method, and a support or removal contact.</p> <p>Before enabling write actions or publishing a new connected capability, verify its role scope and test with an account that has only the intended permissions in the connected service.</p> <p>For a broad rollout, begin with categories teams use every day, such as email, calendar, and file or document systems. Use the <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Plugins Directory (online)</a> to confirm current availability and capabilities across supported ChatGPT and Codex surfaces.</p> <p>Whatever the initial set, start with read actions. Before enabling write actions, identify the plugin owner, review MCP server scopes and service permissions, confirm data access, and document external effects and a recovery path.</p> <h2 id=\"understand-data-flow-and-security\">Understand data flow and security</h2> <p>When ChatGPT uses an MCP server included with a plugin, it sends a request to the connected service and returns data or action results allowed by the authenticated account's permissions in that service.</p> <p>ChatGPT handles data from connected services in two ways:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Non-synced:</strong> ChatGPT processes data from Chat and deep research transiently and doesn't index it.</li> <li><strong>Synced:</strong> ChatGPT indexes selected connected content in advance. You can see whether a connection supports sync on its plugin page.</li> </ul> <p>The mode changes how ChatGPT indexes connected content; it doesn't replace normal chat-retention controls. ChatGPT conversations that use these connections remain available through the Compliance API.</p> <p>OpenAI's connected-service guidance documents encryption in transit and at rest, per-user authorization, role and action controls, restricted network access for conversations that use these connections, and no model training on information accessed through these connections for Business, Enterprise, and Edu customers. When a request reaches a connected service, that service's scopes, retention, data residency, and other policies also apply.</p> <p>See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">security and compliance for connected services (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10847137\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">connections with sync (online)</a> for current data-handling details. For locally configured MCP servers in the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, or IDE extension, see <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Codex MCP configuration</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"use-current-procedures-and-references\">Use current procedures and references</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11509118\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin controls, security, and compliance in apps (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11487775\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Apps in ChatGPT (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10847137\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Apps with sync (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8411955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Manage workspace settings (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">Skills and plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">Admin rollout guide</a></li> </ul>"};
